msgstr "この Masterclass は、2022年3月28日に Luigi Bonati によって作成された。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:7
msgid "Aims"
msgstr "目的"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:9
msgid ""
"This Masterclass describes how to design data-driven collective variables "
"using machine learning (ML) methods."
msgstr ""
"この Masterclass では、Machine Learning（ML）を使って Data-driven な Collective "
"Variables を設計する方法を説明する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:11
msgid "Objectives"
msgstr "到達目標"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:13
msgid "Once this Masterclass is completed, you will know how to:"
msgstr "この Masterclass を終えると、次のことができるようになる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:15
msgid "Design data-driven CVs in Python using Pytorch"
msgstr "Python と PyTorch を使って Data-driven な CVs を設計する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:16
msgid "Deploy them in PLUMED via the PYTORCH_MODEL interface"
msgstr "PYTORCH_MODEL インターフェースを通じて PLUMED で利用する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:18
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr "前提条件"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:20
msgid ""
"We assume that you are familiar with PLUMED and enhanced sampling "
"calculations. If you are not, the 2021 PLUMED Masterclass is a great place "
"to start. We will also use OPES to enhance sampling, which has been covered "
"in another masterclass."
msgstr ""
"PLUMED と Enhanced Sampling 計算に習熟していることを前提とする。初めての場合は、2021年の PLUMED "
"Masterclass がよい出発点になる。Sampling の促進には、別の Masterclass で扱った OPES も用いる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:22
msgid "Furthermore, Python knowledge is required for this masterclass."
msgstr "また、この Masterclass には Python の知識が必要である。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:24
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "概要"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:26
msgid ""
"The identification of suitable collective variables (CVs) is crucial for the"
" success of several enhanced sampling methods. Typically, the quest for CVs "
"has been driven by physical intuition, however, the complexity of the "
"systems that can be simulated nowadays calls for new approaches. For this "
"reason, here we want to learn the CVs directly from molecular dynamics data."
" As in any machine learning approach, the three key ingredients will be (1) "
"the data, (2) the model, and (3) the objective function. We note that these "
"are tightly connected to each other. Indeed, depending on the kind of data "
"that is available we can ask different questions. Furthermore, the ability "
"to answer such questions (as well as to interpret the results) will depend "
"on the choice of appropriate models."
msgstr ""
"適切な Collective Variables（CVs）の特定は、多くの Enhanced Sampling "
"法を成功させるうえで極めて重要である。従来、CVs "
"の探索は物理的直感に基づくことが多かったが、現在シミュレーションできる系の複雑さには新しい方法が必要である。そこで、ここでは MD データから CVs "
"を直接学習する。Machine Learning の他の応用と同様に、重要な要素は (1) データ、(2) モデル、(3) Objective "
"Function "
"の3つである。これらは密接に関係している。利用できるデータの種類によって、問えることが異なるからである。また、その問いに答えられるか、結果を解釈できるかは、適切なモデルの選択に依存する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:29
msgid ""
"Broadly speaking, the CVs should represent the collective atomic movement as"
" the system translocates from one metastable state to another. As a general "
"requirement, CVs should be continuous and differentiable functions of the "
"atomic positions able to (1) distinguish the different states and (2) be "
"connected to the slow modes of the system. However, this results in a "
"chicken and egg problem: if we have reactive trajectories that already "
"explored the relevant phase space we might analyze such simulations and "
"extract good CVs. But more often than not, for obtaining such reactive "
"simulations we already need good CVs. Here we describe two possible ways out"
" of this chicken-and-egg situation, which reflects two scenarios that in the"
" practice occur very often:"
msgstr ""
"大まかに言えば、CVs は、系が1つの Metastable State から別の状態へ移るときの、原子の集団的な運動を表す必要がある。一般に、CVs "
"は原子座標の連続かつ微分可能な関数であり、(1) 異なる状態を区別し、(2) 系の Slow Modes "
"と結び付いていることが求められる。しかし、ここには循環した問題がある。重要な Phase Space を探索済みの Reactive "
"Trajectories があれば、それを解析してよい CVs を取り出せる。一方、そのような Reactive Simulations "
"を得るためには、すでによい CVs が必要なことが多い。ここでは、実際によく生じる2つの状況に対応した、この問題から抜け出す方法を説明する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:34
msgid ""
"(1) Only the metastable states are known. These could be for instance the "
"reactant and product of a chemical reaction, crystalline and liquid "
"configurations of a material, the bound and unbound states of a ligand into "
"a protein, etc... Given this limited data, we can guess the CVs by "
"optimizing variables with a classification criterion. This consists of "
"enforcing only the first CV requirement stated above. Of course, one should "
"not expect this to work as well as if one could add dynamic information on "
"the transition paths, but it should be seen as a way to make the best out of"
" limited knowledge. Very often the only information available is what the "
"states of interest are, and so it is necessary to develop methods that can "
"construct approximate CVs from this information."
msgstr ""
"(1) Metastable States のみが分かっている場合。例えば、化学反応の Reactant と Product、物質の結晶と液体の "
"Configurations、タンパク質に対する Ligand の Bound State と Unbound State "
"などである。限られたデータでも、Classification Criterion で変数を最適化すれば CVs を推定できる。これは、上述の CV "
"の要件のうち最初のものだけを課すことに相当する。当然、Transition Paths "
"の動的な情報も加えられる場合と同じ性能は期待できないが、限られた知識を最大限活用する方法と捉えるべきである。関心のある状態が何かという情報しか得られないことは多く、その情報から近似的な"
" CVs を構成する手法が必要になる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:36
msgid ""
"(2) We have an enhanced sampling simulation in which we have biased some CV,"
" but with suboptimal results. Instead of proceeding by trial and error by "
"changing the CVs until we find the right one(s), we can analyze such "
"simulations and identify the slow degrees of freedom. If we can express them"
" in a functional form and subsequently bias them we will be able to "
"significantly improve sampling quality."
msgstr ""
"(2) ある CV に Bias を加えた Enhanced Sampling シミュレーションはあるが、結果が最適でない場合。適切な CVs "
"が見つかるまで変更を繰り返す代わりに、そのシミュレーションを解析して遅い自由度を特定できる。それを関数として表し、Bias "
"を加えられれば、Sampling の質を大きく改善できる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:38
msgid "Software and data"
msgstr "ソフトウェアとデータ"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:40
msgid ""
"The data needed to complete the exercises of this Masterclass can be found "
"on [GitHub](https://github.com/luigibonati/masterclass-plumed/). To complete"
" the exercises, we will go through a set of **Jupyter notebooks**, from "
"which all the simulations can be performed and analyzed."
msgstr ""
"この Masterclass の演習に必要なデータは "
"[GitHub](https://github.com/luigibonati/masterclass-plumed/) にある。演習では一連の "
"**Jupyter Notebooks** を用い、そこからすべてのシミュレーションを実行・解析できる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:43
msgid ""
"Here you can find the "
"[instructions](https://github.com/luigibonati/masterclass-"
"plumed/blob/main/INSTALL.md) for installing the required software. In "
"particular, you will need to use the development version of PLUMED compiled "
"with LibTorch, as well as GROMACS. To run the simulations we will use "
"GROMACS 2020.6 patched with PLUMED."
msgstr ""
"必要なソフトウェアのインストール[手順](https://github.com/luigibonati/masterclass-"
"plumed/blob/main/INSTALL.md)はこちらにある。特に、LibTorch を有効にしてコンパイルした PLUMED "
"の開発版と、GROMACS が必要である。シミュレーションには、PLUMED のパッチを適用した GROMACS 2020.6 を用いる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:47
msgid "Training CVs with Pytorch"
msgstr "PyTorch による CVs の学習"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:49
msgid ""
"In this tutorial, we will use "
"[mlcvs](https://mlcvs.readthedocs.io/en/latest/), a Python-based package "
"designed for building data-driven collective variables for enhanced sampling"
" simulations. In `mlcvs` we have implemented different kinds of data-driven "
"CVs proposed in the literature, including Deep-LDA and Deep-TICA which we "
"describe in this masterclass."
msgstr ""
"このチュートリアルでは、Enhanced Sampling シミュレーション向けの Data-driven な Collective Variables"
" を作成する Python パッケージ [mlcvs](https://mlcvs.readthedocs.io/en/latest/) "
"を使う。`mlcvs` には、文献で提案された各種の Data-driven CVs を実装しており、この Masterclass で説明する "
"Deep-LDA と Deep-TICA も含まれる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:52
msgid ""
"[!IMPORTANT] The mlcvs library has been renamed to "
"[mlcolvar](https://mlcolvar.readthedocs.io) and integrated with many other "
"functionalities. An older version compatible with the masterclass can be "
"accessed by cloning the `pre-lightning` from the Github "
"[repository](https://github.com/luigibonati/mlcolvar/). However, we suggest "
"to check out the new mlcolvar documentation for up-to-date tutorials and "
"examples for DeepLDA/DeepTICA CVs."
msgstr ""
"[!IMPORTANT] mlcvs ライブラリは [mlcolvar](https://mlcolvar.readthedocs.io) "
"に改称され、多くの機能が統合された。この Masterclass と互換性のある旧版は、GitHub "
"[repository](https://github.com/luigibonati/mlcolvar/) の `pre-lightning` を "
"clone すれば利用できる。ただし、DeepLDA／DeepTICA CVs の最新のチュートリアルや例については、新しい mlcolvar "
"のドキュメントを参照することを勧める。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:57
msgid "Using the CVs in PLUMED"
msgstr "PLUMED で CVs を使う"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:59
msgid ""
"Once the models have been trained on the data, we can export them using the "
"jit (just in time) compiler of Pytorch. This creates a Python-independent "
"model, which can be loaded in PLUMED using Pytorch C++ APIs (LibTorch). Of "
"particular relevance is that we can exploit the automatic differentiation "
"feature of Pytorch to compute derivatives of the model with respect to the "
"inputs. Note that in this way we can load the models exported from `mlcvs` "
"as well as any other function built using Pytorch methods and serialized "
"with jit."
msgstr ""
"データからモデルを学習したら、PyTorch の JIT（Just-in-time）Compiler を用いて export できる。これにより "
"Python に依存しないモデルが作られ、PyTorch C++ APIs（LibTorch）を使って PLUMED "
"に読み込める。特に重要なのは、PyTorch の Automatic Differentiation "
"を利用して、入力に対するモデルの微分を計算できることである。この方法なら、`mlcvs` から export したモデルだけでなく、PyTorch "
"の機能で構成し、JIT で Serialize した他の関数も読み込める。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:62
msgid ""
"A typical PLUMED input might be the following, in which we first calculate "
"some descriptors and feed them as inputs of the model."
msgstr "典型的な PLUMED 入力は次のようになる。まず Descriptors を計算し、それをモデルの入力として渡す。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:72
msgid "Exercises"
msgstr "演習"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:74
msgid ""
"The exercises are presented in the two Jupyter notebooks, from which all the"
" simulations can be performed and analyzed. For this reason, this page only "
"presents a high level overview of the contents of the notebooks."
msgstr ""
"演習は2つの Jupyter Notebooks にあり、すべてのシミュレーションをそこから実行・解析できる。このため、このページでは "
"Notebooks の内容の概要だけを示す。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:77
msgid "Toy system: alanine dipeptide"
msgstr "Toy System：Alanine Dipeptide"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:79
msgid ""
"As done in some previous masterclass, we will play with a toy system, the "
"small alanine dipeptide molecule in a vacuum (ala2). This has the advantage "
"of being a well-known system and it is cheap to simulate. The typical use "
"case is to test enhanced sampling methods using as CVs the torsional angle "
"$\\phi$ and $\\psi$. Since the former is an almost ideal CV for describing "
"the transition between its two metastable states, this will typically result"
" in a very efficient sampling. Here we want to approach this problem in a "
"more blind way and try to design efficient CVs with as little knowledge as "
"possible, learning the CVs directly from the output of molecular dynamics "
"simulations."
msgstr ""
"以前のいくつかの Masterclass と同様に、真空中の小さな Alanine Dipeptide 分子（ala2）を Toy System "
"として使う。よく知られた系で、シミュレーションが低コストという利点がある。典型的には、Torsion Angles の $\\phi$ と "
"$\\psi$ を CVs として Enhanced Sampling 法を試す。前者は2つの Metastable States "
"間の遷移を記述するほぼ理想的な CV なので、通常は非常に効率よく Sampling できる。ここでは、できるだけ事前知識を使わず、MD "
"シミュレーションの出力から CVs を直接学習して、効率的な CVs を設計する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:84
msgid ""
"In both exercises, we will characterize the molecule with a general set of "
"physical descriptors, which are the interatomic distances between heavy "
"atoms. The reason for not working directly with atomic positions is twofold:"
" on one hand, invariant CVs can be easily obtained under the relevant "
"symmetries, while on the other, we can use different kind of descriptors to "
"focus the sampling on the relevant processes."
msgstr ""
"両方の演習では、Heavy Atoms 間の原子間距離という、一般的な物理的 Descriptors "
"の集合で分子を特徴付ける。原子座標を直接用いない理由は2つある。重要な対称性に対して不変な CVs を容易に得られることと、Descriptors "
"の種類を選ぶことで、重要な過程に Sampling を集中させられることである。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:87
msgid "Tutorial 1: `Collective variables from equilibrium fluctuations"
msgstr "チュートリアル1：Equilibrium Fluctuations から求める Collective Variables"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:89
msgid ""
"You can find the first tutorial in the jupyter notebook "
"`tutorial1_DeepLDA.ipynb`. In this exercise, we will design the CVs starting"
" only from a realization of the metastable states. The main steps will be "
"the following:"
msgstr ""
"最初のチュートリアルは Jupyter Notebook `tutorial1_DeepLDA.ipynb` にある。この演習では、Metastable"
" States の実現例のみから CVs を設計する。主な手順は次のとおりである。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:92
msgid ""
"Perform short unbiased MD simulations in the metastable states and evaluate "
"a set of physical descriptors (e.g. interatomic distances between heavy "
"atoms)"
msgstr ""
"Metastable States で短い Unbiased MD を実行し、物理的 Descriptors の集合（Heavy Atoms "
"間の距離など）を評価する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:93
msgid ""
"We train a neural-network based CV to discriminate between the states, using"
" Fisher's discriminant as the objective function (DeepLDA)"
msgstr ""
"Fisher Discriminant を Objective Function として、状態を識別する Neural Network に基づく CV "
"を学習する（DeepLDA）。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:94
msgid ""
"Finally, we apply a bias potential to enhance the fluctuations of the "
"DeepLDA CV and drive the system back and forth between the two states."
msgstr "最後に BiasPotential を加え、DeepLDA CV のゆらぎを増強して、2つの状態間を行き来させる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:96
msgid "Tutorial 2: Collective variables as slow modes of biased simulations"
msgstr "チュートリアル2：Biased シミュレーションの Slow Modes としての Collective Variables"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:98
msgid ""
"In the second exercise, which you can find in the notebook "
"`tutorial2_DeepTICA.ipynb` , we will extract the CVs from biased "
"simulations. As before, we will go through three main steps:"
msgstr ""
"2つ目の演習は Notebook `tutorial2_DeepTICA.ipynb` にあり、Biased シミュレーションから CVs "
"を取り出す。前と同じく、主に3つの手順で進める。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:100
msgid ""
"Perform an enhanced sampling calculation using some approximate CVs as well "
"as generalized ensembles simulations (e.g. multicanonical)."
msgstr ""
"近似的な CVs を用いた Enhanced Sampling 計算や、Generalized Ensembles "
"シミュレーション（Multicanonical など）を行う。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:101
msgid ""
"Use the trajectory to train a neural-network based CV to find the maximally "
"autocorrelated modes, which correspond to the slowest degrees of freedom "
"(DeepTICA)"
msgstr ""
"Trajectory を用いて Neural Network に基づく CV を学習し、最も遅い自由度に対応する、Autocorrelation "
"が最大の Modes を見つける（DeepTICA）。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:102
msgid "Bias these slow degrees of freedom to improve sampling"
msgstr "これらの遅い自由度に Bias を加え、Sampling を改善する。"
